[0.000, "o", "diff --git a/docs/verification/ux-audit-signup-2026-11-05/evidence/contrast.py b/docs/verification/ux-audit-signup-2026-11-05/evidence/contrast.py\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..fa3d5082af0590fbb8adf8a4874914b0a3fa9a7a\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/docs/verification/ux-audit-signup-2026-11-05/evidence/contrast.py\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@\r\n+from pathlib import Path\r\n+import json\r\n+def luminance(h):\r\n+    c = [int(h[i:i+2], 16)/255 for i in (0, 2, 4)]\r\n+    c = [v/12.92 if v <= .04045 else ((v+.055)/1.055)**2.4 for v in c]\r\n+    return sum(a*b for a,b in zip(c, (.2126,.7152,.0722)))\r\n+def contrast(a,b):\r\n+    lo,hi = sorted((luminance(a),luminance(b)))\r\n+    return (hi+.05)/(lo+.05)\r\n+for name,a,b in [('body/banner','aaaaaa','ffffff'),('heading','bbbbbb','ffffff'),('signup','ffffff','7fc8f8')]:\r\n+    print(f'{name}: #{a} on #{b} = {contrast(a,b):.4f}:1')\r\n+\r\ndiff --git a/docs/verification/ux-audit-signup-2026-11-05/integrity-check.json b/docs/verification/ux-audit-signup-2026-11-05/inte"]
[0.000, "o", "grity-check.json\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..7fe28264458bd65bbf22fc6db0c842f9393af3ef\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/docs/verification/ux-audit-signup-2026-11-05/integrity-check.json\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@\r\n+{\r\n+  \"wrapperMatches\": true,\r\n+  \"lockHashMatches\": true,\r\n+  \"installedIntegritiesMatch\": true,\r\n+  \"startingCheckedAt\": \"2026-11-05T18:56:40.144Z\",\r\n+  \"finalCheckedAt\": \"2026-11-05T18:58:49.404Z\"\r\n+}\r\ndiff --git a/docs/verification/ux-audit-signup-2026-11-05/report.md b/docs/verification/ux-audit-signup-2026-11-05/report.md\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..6c7e159137d85218eddb45cc6e56b71cbc0831cc\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/docs/verification/ux-audit-signup-2026-11-05/report.md\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,167 @@\r\n+# Signup UX audit — 2026-11-05\r\n+\r\n+The first priority is to make signup produce an honest, reachable result. The supplied page is explicitly a synthetic demo; its action only opens “Thanks!”, without reading credentials or creating an accoun"]
[0.000, "o", "t. Keyboard access and text contrast also need attention before this becomes a usable signup flow.\r\n+\r\n+## Scope and evidence\r\n+\r\n+- Repository: local `sam-ux-audit-demo`, commit `35507bde01e86dc39cbcb80df831f3b459607c94`; working tree initially clean.\r\n+- Entire tracked repository: `index.html`, 28 lines. No README, AGENTS.md, package manifest, setup instructions, backend, or bundled `hero.jpg` found.\r\n+- Assumed user: a new visitor seeking a meal-planning account; primary task: enter credentials, sign up, understand the result and next step.\r\n+- Platform: public web, desktop/mobile, keyboard/pointer/assistive technology. Audience and product stage beyond the explicit demo comment are unknown.\r\n+- Mode: artifact-limited repository review. Source observation and CSS calculations support the findings; user effects are source-based inferences, not reproduced browser behavior.\r\n+- Environment: local zsh workspace, Python 3 for calculations, npm for skill preflight. No approved browser/DevTools tool was exposed. "]
[0.000, "o", "No local preview, browser automation, Lighthouse, axe, screen reader, screenshots, or recordings were run.\r\n+- URL/viewport: none exercised. Runtime focus, accessibility tree, actual rendered contrast, reflow, target geometry, animation playback, delays, recovery, and account creation remain unverified.\r\n+- Site source was not changed. Audit artifacts are the only additions.\r\n+- Starting dependency receipt: [skill-versions.json](skill-versions.json). Final receipt: [skill-versions-final.json](skill-versions-final.json). Verification outcome is recorded in [integrity-check.json](integrity-check.json).\r\n+- Snapshot: [evidence/index.html.txt](evidence/index.html.txt), preserving source line numbers. Source SHA-256: `0e881e50de686959ac92b952235d198c7812f826e2066583efe79f5a213431bb`. Reproduce color calculations with `python3 docs/verification/ux-audit-signup-2026-11-05/evidence/contrast.py`.\r\n+\r\n+### Lens coverage\r\n+\r\n+| Locked dependency | Status and coverage |\r\n+| --- | --- |\r\n+| `.runtime/skills/a11y/SKILL.md`"]
[0.000, "o", " | Reviewed: source semantics, keyboard implementation, labels, colors, language, image alternatives. Runtime accessibility checks blocked by unavailable browser tools. |\r\n+| `.runtime/skills/hig/SKILL.md` | Reviewed: transferable hierarchy, clarity, feedback, data entry and control principles only. Read accessibility, color, typography, layout, entering-data and feedback references. Native Apple conventions do not apply to this web page. |\r\n+| `.runtime/skills/motion/SKILL.md` | Reviewed: banner animation source, continuous movement and missing preference handling. Playback, repeat use and interruption checks blocked. |\r\n+| `.runtime/skills/performance/SKILL.md` | Not applicable: performance not requested; no live delay evidence. No general optimization audit launched. |\r\n+| `.runtime/skills/core-web-vitals/SKILL.md` | Not applicable: no performance measurement requiring this supporting lens. |\r\n+\r\n+## Prioritized findings\r\n+\r\n+Severity describes task harm; confidence describes evidence strength. No finding "]
[0.000, "o", "is a claim of a completed WCAG conformance assessment.\r\n+\r\n+### 1. Signup acknowledges an action without creating an account\r\n+\r\n+**Severity: High. Confidence: High. Lenses: feedback, recovery, HIG.**\r\n+\r\n+**User/task/state:** Any new visitor activating signup, with empty, invalid or valid-looking credentials.\r\n+\r\n+**Source observation:** [index.html:21–26](../../../index.html#L21) defines inputs and a click handler whose entire body is `alert('Thanks!')`. There is no form, input read, validation, request, persistence or next screen in the repository.\r\n+\r\n+**Impact (source-inferred):** The core task cannot complete in this implementation; the acknowledgment offers no useful next step and may be interpreted as success. Loading, failure and retry feedback are absent because there is no account operation.\r\n+\r\n+**Smallest recommendation:** If this remains a demo, visibly label the action as a preview and state that no account was created. Before using it for real signup, connect a form to the intended account s"]
[0.000, "o", "ervice and distinguish pending, validation failure, service failure and confirmed success. Avoid adding unnecessary setup.\r\n+\r\n+**Acceptance check:** In a safe test environment, empty/invalid values receive actionable feedback; service failure preserves useful input and permits retry; a successful response produces a verifiable account outcome and next step. The demo path explicitly says no account is created.\r\n+\r\n+### 2. The primary action has no keyboard or button implementation\r\n+\r\n+**Severity: High. Confidence: High. Lenses: accessibility, control.**\r\n+\r\n+**User/task/state:** A keyboard or assistive-technology user attempting signup after entering credentials.\r\n+\r\n+**Source observation:** `index.html:23` uses a `div onclick` with no button role, tabindex or keyboard handler. There is also no form submission path. `index.html:12` removes its focus outline.\r\n+\r\n+**Impact (source-inferred):** The action is excluded from normal Tab navigation and lacks native keyboard activation and button semantics. The outl"]
[0.000, "o", "ine rule is a latent problem if focusability alone is patched; it is not evidence of a separately observed invisible focus state.\r\n+\r\n+**Smallest recommendation:** Use a native submit button in a form with a visible focus indicator. This supplies familiar semantics and keyboard behavior with less custom code.\r\n+\r\n+**Acceptance check:** Tab reaches the action; focus is visible; Enter submits from an appropriate field; Enter/Space activate the focused button once; the accessibility tree identifies a named button.\r\n+\r\n+**Standard:** Source indicates failures of [WCAG 2.1.1 Keyboard (A)](https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/#keyboard) and [4.1.2 Name, Role, Value (A)](https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/#name-role-value).\r\n+\r\n+### 3. Key text colors have insufficient contrast\r\n+\r\n+**Severity: High. Confidence: High for declared-color calculations; runtime unverified. Lenses: accessibility, visual hierarchy.**\r\n+\r\n+**User/task/state:** A visitor reading the offer, heading or signup action, especially with low vision.\r\n+\r\n+**Sour"]
[0.000, "o", "ce observation:** `index.html:7–11` specifies the following opaque sRGB pairs:\r\n+\r\n+| Text | Foreground/background | Calculated contrast |\r\n+| --- | --- | --- |\r\n+| Body/banner | #aaa / #fff | 2.32:1 |\r\n+| Heading | #bbb / #fff | 1.92:1 |\r\n+| Signup, 11 CSS px | #fff / #7fc8f8 | 1.82:1 |\r\n+\r\n+**Impact (source-inferred):** Weak text contrast makes the purpose and primary action harder to read. These are calculations from CSS, not sampled browser pixels. Input text/placeholder contrast was not measured.\r\n+\r\n+**Smallest recommendation:** Darken the text or action background while retaining the existing simple hierarchy. Verify chosen pairs rather than prescribing a new visual identity.\r\n+\r\n+**Acceptance check:** Normal text reaches 4.5:1 and qualifying large text 3:1 in all relevant rendered states. The heading pair fails even the lower threshold, regardless of its final font weight.\r\n+\r\n+**Standard:** [WCAG 1.4.3 Contrast (Minimum), AA](https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/#contrast-minimum).\r\n+\r\n+### 4. Banner movem"]
[0.000, "o", "ent continues without user control\r\n+\r\n+**Severity: Medium. Confidence: High for source; perceived effect unverified. Lenses: motion, accessibility, attention.**\r\n+\r\n+**User/task/state:** Someone trying to read or enter credentials while the offer banner moves.\r\n+\r\n+**Source observation:** `index.html:13–14,18` applies `slide 0.4s infinite alternate`, translating between −10px and +10px. The file supplies neither pause/stop control nor reduced-motion handling.\r\n+\r\n+**Impact (source-inferred):** Continuous decorative movement competes with the signup task and offers no demonstrated task benefit.\r\n+\r\n+**Smallest recommendation:** Make the offer static. If motion is retained for a justified purpose, provide a way to stop it and respect reduced-motion preferences.\r\n+\r\n+**Acceptance check:** Observe the page beyond five seconds and with reduced motion enabled; no uncontrolled decorative movement remains and the offer is still readable.\r\n+\r\n+**Standard:** Source indicates [WCAG 2.2.2 Pause, Stop, Hide (A)](http"]
[0.000, "o", "s://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/#pause-stop-hide): automatic nonessential movement continuing beyond five seconds alongside other content needs a pause, stop or hide mechanism. No timing or smoothness claim was tested.\r\n+\r\n+### 5. Field identity disappears during entry; input purposes are underspecified\r\n+\r\n+**Severity: Medium. Confidence: High for markup; assistive-technology effects unverified. Lenses: accessibility, data entry.**\r\n+\r\n+**User/task/state:** A visitor entering or correcting credentials, or using autofill/mobile input.\r\n+\r\n+**Source observation:** `index.html:21–22` provides placeholder-only identification, without persistent labels, IDs, names or autocomplete tokens. Email defaults to a text input; password is appropriately masked.\r\n+\r\n+**Impact (source-inferred):** Field prompts disappear once text is entered. Email keyboard/validation affordances and explicit autofill purpose are absent. Placeholders may provide fallback accessible names in some browser/AT combinations; this report does not asse"]
[0.000, "o", "rt that both fields are unnamed.\r\n+\r\n+**Smallest recommendation:** Add associated visible labels, `type=\"email\"`, stable names and appropriate `autocomplete=\"email\"` / `\"new-password\"`. State actual password requirements if the eventual service has them.\r\n+\r\n+**Acceptance check:** Labels persist for filled fields; each field has the expected accessible name and purpose; mobile email input and password-manager filling work. Check actual validation behavior with finding 1.\r\n+\r\n+### 6. Page identity and language metadata are missing or generic\r\n+\r\n+**Severity: Medium. Confidence: High. Lens: accessibility, orientation.**\r\n+\r\n+**User/task/state:** A screen-reader user opening the page or anyone locating the signup tab again.\r\n+\r\n+**Source observation:** `index.html:3` has no `lang`; `index.html:5` sets the document title to “Page.”\r\n+\r\n+**Impact (source-inferred):** The document does not identify its default language, and its title does not distinguish meal-planning signup.\r\n+\r\n+**Smallest recommendation:** D"]
[0.000, "o", "eclare `lang=\"en\"` for this English page and use a descriptive signup title including the real product name when known.\r\n+\r\n+**Acceptance check:** Inspect document metadata and browser tab; screen-reader language selection follows the declared language and the tab identifies its purpose.\r\n+\r\n+**Standards:** [WCAG 3.1.1 Language of Page (A)](https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/#language-of-page), [2.4.2 Page Titled (A)](https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/#page-titled).\r\n+\r\n+### 7. Hero image reference cannot be satisfied by this repository\r\n+\r\n+**Severity: Low. Confidence: High for missing local asset; deployment behavior unknown. Lenses: content, accessibility.**\r\n+\r\n+**User/task/state:** A new visitor viewing the signup page.\r\n+\r\n+**Source observation:** `index.html:25` references `hero.jpg` without an `alt` attribute; the only tracked file is `index.html` and the local image does not exist.\r\n+\r\n+**Impact (source-inferred):** A straightforward static serving of this checkout cannot supply that image. Its intended content"]
[0.000, "o", " and importance are unknown; a deployed server might supply an asset separately.\r\n+\r\n+**Smallest recommendation:** Remove the image if unnecessary, or provide the intended asset with descriptive alternative text if informative and `alt=\"\"` if decorative.\r\n+\r\n+**Acceptance check:** Confirm the asset resolves in the deployed preview and its accessible treatment matches its purpose. No essential signup information depends on it.\r\n+\r\n+## Strengths to preserve\r\n+\r\n+- `index.html:20` states a concrete benefit, “Plan meals in minutes.”\r\n+- Only two credential fields and one primary action are presented (`21–23`); retain this limited entry burden unless product requirements justify more.\r\n+- The password input uses native masking (`22`). No custom paste-blocking code appears; password-manager behavior still needs runtime verification.\r\n+\r\n+## Disagreements and limits\r\n+\r\n+The wrapper's evidence-based severity rubric takes precedence over dependency defaults that label all accessibility defects Critical. Here ke"]
[0.000, "o", "yboard exclusion and unreadable primary content merit High; there is no demonstrated severe irreversible harm. The motion dependency's universal timing/easing defaults and preference for retaining some motion are review prompts, not web requirements: removing this decoration is appropriate. Native Apple point sizes and platform conventions were not imposed.\r\n+\r\n+Missing viewport metadata (`index.html:4–16`) is a mobile validation risk, not proof of a reproduced reflow failure. Actual target size, border visibility, zoom and overflow remain unchecked. No numeric target-size failure, frame-rate problem, conversion effect, deceptive-offer allegation or flash/seizure claim is made.\r\n+\r\n+The copy “Limited offer!” gives no details (`18`), but no price, billing or commitment exists in the implementation. Whether the offer is meaningful, whether visitors understand the product, and whether signup should precede a meal-planning preview are user hypotheses. Do not invent commercial terms or demand a particular ac"]
[0.000, "o", "quisition flow.\r\n+\r\n+## Ordered next actions\r\n+\r\n+1. Decide whether this is an explicitly labeled preview or a real signup flow; address finding 1 accordingly.\r\n+2. Make the primary task keyboard-accessible and legible; address findings 2–3.\r\n+3. Remove continuous banner motion; add persistent field labels and purpose metadata.\r\n+4. Correct document identity and resolve or remove the image.\r\n+5. Validate the result in a browser: keyboard/AT, narrow mobile layout, zoom/reflow, reduced motion, valid/invalid input, service failure/retry and confirmed success in a test environment. No account operation was executed in this audit.\r\n+\r\n+Then ask an intended meal-planning user to explain what they expect after signup and attempt the task. Observe understanding, field corrections and recognition of completion; use that evidence to decide whether value demonstration or offer clarification is needed. No participant results are claimed.\r\n+\r\ndiff --git a/docs/verification/ux-audit-signup-2026-11-05/skill-versions-final"]
